      "content": [],
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A study established that in a certain park, there are at least 141 squirrels, consisting of red\nsquirrels and gray squirrels. The study also established that there are at least 4 times as many gray\nsquirrels as red squirrels in this park. Which of the following systems of inequalities best\nrepresents this situation, where $g$ is the number of gray squirrels in this park and $r$ is the number\nof red squirrels in this park?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-bb67b9ec4d634df59ab5855ac17fb387",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q5"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$g+r \\le 141$ , $g \\ge 4 r$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$g+r \\le 141$ , $g \\le 4 r$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$g+r \\ge 141$ , $g \\ge 4 r$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$g+r \\ge 141$ , $g \\le 4 r$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
