        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Triangle $ABC$ is similar to triangle $XYZ$ such that $A$, $B$, and $C$ correspond to $X$, $Y$, and $Z$,\nrespectively. The length of each side of triangle $ABC$ is $n$ times the length of its corresponding\nside in triangle $XYZ$, where $n$ is an integer greater than 1 . The measure of angle $C$ is 52 degrees,\nand $YZ=71$. Which of the following must be true?"
        }
